 "last_activity": "2014-10-10T11:48:48Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "H3Ljo6p7B08J",
   "from": "Boby Mathew",
   "author": "6aa00cba374c488a",
   "date": "2014-10-07T07:51:44Z",
   "subject": "Imputation",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hello<p>I was wondering is it possible to use haley knott regression method to impute the missing data in r/QTL. Because I need the imputed data for MCMC analysis.<p>thanks,<p>Boby Mathew</p></p></p>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Lnjqm-UzGEEJ",
   "from": "Karl Broman",
   "author": "96353e7106735838",
   "date": "2014-10-07T11:43:32Z",
   "subject": "Re: Imputation",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Haley-Knott regression is a method for QTL analysis; I can&#39;t think of a way that it can be used as a method to impute missing data.<div><br></div><div>To impute missing genotype data, use fill.geno(). There are three options:</div><div><br></div><div>  - &quot;imp&quot;: take a random draw from Pr(genotype | marker data)</div><div>  - &quot;argmax&quot;: choose the sequence of genotypes for which Pr(genotypes | marker data) is maximal</div><div>  - &quot;no_dbl_XO&quot;: missing values between two matching genotypes (non-recombinant) are filled in with that match; missing values between recombinant genotypes are left missing</div><div><br></div><div>karl</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Tuesday, October 7, 2014 2:51:44 AM UTC-5, Boby Mathew wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">Hello<p>I was wondering is it possible to use haley knott regression method to impute the missing data in r/QTL. Because I need the imputed data for MCMC analysis.</p><p>thanks,</p><p>Boby Mathew</p><p></p><p></p></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "8en8Qp0hF7gJ",
   "from": "Karl Broman",
   "author": "96353e7106735838",
   "date": "2014-10-07T12:27:49Z",
   "subject": "Re: Imputation",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">In the development version of R/qtl, I&#39;ve added a new option for fill.geno, method=&quot;maxmarginal&quot;. At each marker, it picks the genotype with maximum probability (provided this exceeds a chosen threshold, min.prob).<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><p></p><p></p></blockquote><div><br></div><div>The key code is at <a href=\"https://github.com/kbroman/qtl/blob/devel/R/util.R#L1858-L1867\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/kbroman/qtl/blob/devel/R/util.R%23L1858-L1867&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792448364844000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1CCBKBBTItjTOZkyGGPcmE\">https://github.com/kbroman/qtl/blob/devel/R/util.R#L1858-L1867</a></div><div><br></div><div>You could do this &quot;by hand&quot; as follows:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">temp </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> calc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">genoprob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cross</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> error</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.01</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">chr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    p </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> temp$geno</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">$prob<br>    whmax </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> apply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">p</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> which</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">max</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    maxpr </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> apply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">p</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> max</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    g </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cross$geno</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">$data<br>    g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">maxpr </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> min</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> whmax</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">maxpr </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> min</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    cross$geno</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">$data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> g<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div>karl</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "fXBFxEXkCl8J",
   "from": "Boby Mathew",
   "author": "6aa00cba374c488a",
   "date": "2014-10-07T13:17:40Z",
   "subject": "Re: Imputation",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Dear Prof. Karl Broman,<br><br><br>Thanks for the code and the detailed explanation. <br>I have a small question does this  probability is calculated conditional on the known flanking genotypes?. <br><br>Boby Mathew</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Tuesday, October 7, 2014 2:27:49 PM UTC+2, Karl Broman wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">In the development version of R/qtl, I&#39;ve added a new option for fill.geno, method=&quot;maxmarginal&quot;. At each marker, it picks the genotype with maximum probability (provided this exceeds a chosen threshold, min.prob).<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><p></p><p></p></blockquote><div><br></div><div>The key code is at <a href=\"https://github.com/kbroman/qtl/blob/devel/R/util.R#L1858-L1867\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/kbroman/qtl/blob/devel/R/util.R%23L1858-L1867&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792448364847000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0AYG4GLWpWSpovUnXfmxCK\">https://github.com/kbroman/qtl/blob/devel/R/util.R#L1858-L1867</a></div><div><br></div><div>You could do this &quot;by hand&quot; as follows:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">temp </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> calc</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">genoprob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">cross</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> error</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.01</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#008\">for</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i </span><span style=\"color:#008\">in</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\">n</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">chr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">{</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    p </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> temp$geno</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">$prob<br>    whmax </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> apply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">p</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> which</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">max</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    maxpr </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> apply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">p</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> max</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    g </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> cross$geno</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">$data<br>    g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">maxpr </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> min</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> whmax</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">maxpr </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> min</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">prob</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    cross$geno</span><span style=\"color:#660\">[[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">i</span><span style=\"color:#660\">]]</span><span style=\"color:#000\">$data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> g<br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">}</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div>karl</div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "iVl92jU-YS8J",
   "from": "Karl Broman",
   "author": "96353e7106735838",
   "date": "2014-10-10T11:48:48Z",
   "subject": "Re: [Rqtl-disc] Re: Imputation",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "The probabilities are conditional on genotypes for all markers on the chromosome.\r<br>\r<br>karl\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>On Oct 7, 2014, at 8:17 AM, Boby Mathew &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">boby...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:\r<br>\r<br>&gt; Dear Prof. Karl Broman,\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Thanks for the code and the detailed explanation. \r<br>&gt; I have a small question does this  probability is calculated conditional on the known flanking genotypes?. \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Boby Mathew\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; On Tuesday, October 7, 2014 2:27:49 PM UTC+2, Karl Broman wrote:\r<br>&gt; In the development version of R/qtl, I&#39;ve added a new option for fill.geno, method=&quot;maxmarginal&quot;. At each marker, it picks the genotype with maximum probability (provided this exceeds a chosen threshold, min.prob).\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; The key code is at <a href=\"https://github.com/kbroman/qtl/blob/devel/R/util.R#L1858-L1867\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/kbroman/qtl/blob/devel/R/util.R%23L1858-L1867&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792448364848000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0a4ZccCUB3L9qmgSNhVbP_\">https://github.com/kbroman/qtl/blob/devel/R/util.R#L1858-L1867</a>\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; You could do this &quot;by hand&quot; as follows:\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; temp &lt;- calc.genoprob(cross, error.prob=0.01)\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; for(i in 1:n.chr) {\r<br>&gt;     p &lt;- temp$geno[[i]]$prob\r<br>&gt;     whmax &lt;- apply(p, 1:2, which.max)\r<br>&gt;     maxpr &lt;- apply(p, 1:2, max)\r<br>&gt;     g &lt;- cross$geno[[i]]$data\r<br>&gt;     g[maxpr &gt; min.prob] &lt;- whmax[maxpr &gt; min.prob]\r<br>&gt;     cross$geno[[i]]$data &lt;- g\r<br>&gt; }\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; karl\r<br>&gt; \r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
